-- Migrates two more hardcoded content sources into app_content — see
-- 20260828_remote_content_config.sql for the table + RLS policy (public
-- read, admin-write only); this file only adds rows, no schema changes.
--
--   class_topic — one row per lesson topic inside an Academy Classes
--   subject (Reading, Algebra & Functions, Biology, ...). `key` is the
--   subject's registered navigation screen name (see ClassesStack.js).
--   `meta.topic_key` is preserved from the original hardcoded data because
--   it's the same string already written into every user's
--   class_topic_progress rows — add/edit/remove topics here (for existing
--   subjects) and it shows up for everyone with no build. See
--   src/components/ClassTopicScreen.js for the fetch + fallback.
--
--   area_tip — one row per tip shown in a Library life-area section's
--   Tips tab. `key` is the section's screen name (the keys of
--   SECTION_CONFIGS in src/screens/library/AreaSectionScreen.js). Add,
--   edit, or remove tips per section here, same no-build deal.
--
-- Apply this in the Supabase SQL editor, or via `supabase db push`.
-- Re-running this file will insert duplicate rows (app_content has no
-- natural unique key across type/key/title) — only run it once, same as
-- the other migrations in this folder.


